# Project: SafeShare MD — on-device redaction of medical reports before sharing (e.g. to WhatsApp)

Full specification: docs/SPEC.md. Read it before starting any task.

## Non-negotiable privacy rules
1. All processing happens on the user's device, in the browser. There is NO backend that receives user files.
2. Never send user files, images, OCR text or detection results over the network. No fetch / XMLHttpRequest / WebSocket / sendBeacon / form POST carrying user data.
3. No cloud or AI APIs of any kind (OpenAI, Grok, Google Vision, AWS, Azure, etc.).
4. No analytics, telemetry, crash reporting (Sentry etc.), ads, fonts or scripts from third parties.
5. All libraries, WASM files, ML models and OCR language data are self-hosted from our own origin. No CDN loading at runtime.
6. Never persist user images or text: no localStorage, IndexedDB, Cache API or service-worker caching of user data. Only user *settings* may be stored in localStorage.
7. Keep the strict Content Security Policy defined in the spec. Never loosen it without asking me.
8. Output is always a NEW image re-encoded from a canvas: flattened, no metadata, no text layer. Redaction = opaque solid black fill. Never blur or pixelate. Never output a PDF containing a text layer.
9. Never put patient data in filenames, page titles, URLs, console logs or error messages. Strip debug logging of OCR text from production builds.

## Design principles
- Recall over precision: when unsure, redact. Over-redaction is acceptable; a missed identifier is a bug.
- Preserve clinical data: do not redact lab result values, units or reference ranges unless they are clearly an identifier.
- The user must always review and confirm before sharing.

## Coding conventions
- TypeScript (strict), React, Vite. Detection logic lives in small pure functions with unit tests.
- Before adding any dependency, tell me why, and confirm it can be self-hosted and works offline.
- After each task: run lint, typecheck and tests, and fix failures before reporting done.
- If any request conflicts with these rules, stop and ask me instead of proceeding.
